## CSV export for Analytics Spend tab

**Context:** The Spend tab's "Where the money went" card already renders a per-leaf table (project, provider, model, runs, reported, estimated, total) from `AnalyticsSpend.leaves` (`packages/contracts/src/analytics-spend.ts`), loaded client-side via TanStack Query. Since the data is already in the browser, no new backend endpoint is needed — just a pure CSV formatter plus a client-side download trigger.

### 1. `apps/web/src/analytics/spend-csv.ts` (new)
Pure function, no DOM:
```ts
const HEADER = 'project,provider,model,runs,cost_usd,reported_usd,estimated_usd';

function csvField(value: string): string {
  return /[",\n]/.test(value) ? `"${value.replaceAll('"', '""')}"` : value;
}

export function spendCsv(data: AnalyticsSpend): string {
  const rows = data.leaves.map((leaf) =>
    [csvField(leaf.project), csvField(leaf.provider), csvField(leaf.model),
     String(leaf.runs), leaf.costUsd.toFixed(4), leaf.reportedUsd.toFixed(4),
     leaf.estimatedUsd.toFixed(4)].join(','),
  );
  return `${[HEADER, ...rows].join('\n')}\n`;
}
```
- Rows follow `data.leaves` order as given — no re-sorting.
- **Model column uses `leaf.model`** (raw id), not `leaf.modelLabel` (the display name shown in the UI table). This matches the `model` header name and stays stable if display labels change, but flag it for confirmation before merging since the on-screen table uses `modelLabel`.
- Amounts are plain `toFixed(4)` decimals, not `$`-formatted — don't reuse `formatCost`/`usd` from `analytics-model.ts`.
- Only comma/quote/newline trigger RFC 4180 quoting, as specified — no formula-injection neutralization like the existing server-side `apps/server/src/audit/cost-csv.ts` does. Worth a second look since project/provider/model are free text, but not part of what was asked.

### 2. `apps/web/src/analytics/spend-csv.test.ts` (new)
Mirror the style of `apps/server/src/audit/cost-csv.test.ts` and `summaries.test.ts`: header exactly matches, one row per leaf in order, 4-decimal amounts, quoting for comma/quote/newline cases, trailing `\n`, and header-only output for empty `leaves`.

### 3. `SpendTab.tsx` — Export button
Add an "Export CSV" button in the `aside` slot of the first `ChartCard` ("Where the money went"), using `DownloadIcon` from `ui/icons.tsx` (same icon `AuditExport.tsx` uses). On click: build the string with `spendCsv(data)`, wrap in a `Blob`, trigger download via a temporary `<a download>` with an object URL (revoked after), filename like `spend-<window.from>-<window.to>.csv`. Hide/disable when `data.leaves.length === 0`, matching the existing `EmptyChart` branch.

